WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.659
Donald Trump and Hillary Clinton faced off
in the first presidential debate of the season.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.100
Here it is in 3:00 minutes.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.840
They were both terrible in their own unique
ways.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.700
Trump talked a lot about law and order

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.120
and touted New York City’s rights-violating stop-and-frisk policy.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.300
We have to bring back law and order.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.160
Now wether or not, in a place like Chicago,
you do stop and frisk, which worked very well,

00:00:21.169 --> 00:00:23.929
Mayor Giuliani is here, worked very well in
New York.

00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:25.960
It brought the crime rate way down.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.320
Of course, murder rates were going down before
stop-and-frisk, went down during stop-and-frisk,

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:34.510
and have continued to go down after New Yorkers’
right to walk down a sidewalk without being

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.500
intimately touched by an armed agent of the
state was restored.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.760
Clinton’s response was to point at guns...

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.699
We've got too many military-style weapons
on the streets.

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:45.759
In a lot of places our police are out-gunned.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.820
...despite the fact that gun violence is also
at an all-time low nationwide.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.300
Most people watching the debate are going
to remember where the candidates disagreed,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.760
but to libertarians, the perhaps more disturbing areas

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.740
are those where the candidates are in agreement.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.240
Even though Trump talked a big game about
debt reduction...

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:07.000
We owe 20 trillion dollars... 20 trillion
in debt... we're a debtor nation...

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.610
...both agreed that we just don’t spend
enough.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.570
Let's have paid family leave.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.570
Trump tried to outdo Hillary’s $30 billion
a year family leave government mandate...

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.130
As far as child care is concerned and so many
other things

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.430
I think Hillary and I agree on that.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.920
....with his own family leave plan and other
spending proposals that would increase the

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.210
debt by $11.5 trillion over 10 years.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:30.420
Unlike Trump, Clinton acknowledged the possibility
that international trade is a good thing…

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.840
Well I think that trade is an important issue.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.110
Of course, we are 5% of the world's population,
we have to trade with the other 95%.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.910
But after the primary campaign, both candidates
now agree

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.610
that the deals we have are killing us.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.280
You want to approve Trans-Pacific Partnership.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.970
You were totally in favor of it, then you
heard what I was saying, how bad it is, and

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.790
you said 'I can't win that debate.'

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.390
That, that is just not accurate.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.090
I was against it once it was finally negotiated.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Leaving nobody on stage to defend the principle
of free trade.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:05.420
If you're too dangerous to fly, you are too
dangerous to buy a gun.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.330
The most egregious area of total agreement

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.770
was on the issue of gun rights and government lists.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:14.170
Pass a prohibition on anyone who's on the
Terrorist Watch List

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.690
from being able to buy a gun in our country.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.160
I think we have to look very strongly at no-fly
lists and watch lists and when people are

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.760
on there, even if they shouldn't be on there,

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.300
we'll help them, we'll help them legally, we'll help them get off.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.560
Once again, Americans didn’t get a chance
to hear a principled argument

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.500
about individual rights, the Constitution, and due process.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.890
While the debate had its fair share of strange
and entertaining moments….

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.880
I call it... trumped-up trickle-down.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.860
I will release my tax returns against my lawyer's
wishes.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.870
When she releases her 33 thousand emails that
have been deleted.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:54.190
As soon as she releases them, I will release,
I will release, my tax returns.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.620
And that's against my lawyers.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.960
They said 'don't do it.'

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.820
American voters were cheated out of a full
debate that represents the true diversity

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.720
of political thought and opinion that exists
in this country.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.900
Instead, they got what they almost always
get:

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.580
the chance to choose between two bad candidates.

